# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzc.md#position-and-parameters
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0065, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0080, PV-0310, PV-0312, PV-0311
# kind: decompress
# description: Byte 7 gives maxbits 8, below the allowed range.
# derivation: Header: length 1, byte 7 = 8 | 0x80 = 0x88, so maxbits = 0x88 & 0x1F = 8 (PV-0310), outside 9-16 (PV-0080, PV-0311): bad-maxbits before any code is read (IMPL-LZC-4). The data 41 00 is a valid single literal and is never read.
# expect.error: bad-maxbits
# expect.algorithm: lzc
# expect.uncompressed_length: 1
# expect.block_mode: 1
hex:
01 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
11                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
88                                                # byte 7
41 00                                             # never read
